       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is double the labeled maximum of 10 mg per day. Doses above 10 mg add little blood-pressure benefit and raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia.\n\nHow would you like to proceed?\n\n1. **Enter 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Enter 20 mg as written.** I'll do this if you confirm it's intentional, and I can add a note such as \"dose exceeds usual max, confirmed by attending.\"\n3. **Use a different regimen.** If 10 mg isn't controlling BP, you could add a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor/ARB or a thiazide-like diuretic, instead of raising amlodipine further.\n\nLet me know which option you want."
